<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#jihad">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jihad</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jihad is an Islamic term meaning struggle or striving, which can refer to spiritual effort or to armed struggle in defence or expansion of the faith. Armed jihad was a central theme in the founding of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sokoto-caliphate">Sokoto Caliphate</a> and in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saladin">Saladin</a>'s wars against the crusaders in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ayyubid-empire">Ayyubid Empire</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adal-sultanate">Adal Sultanate</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almohad-caliphate">Almohad Caliphate</a> also framed their wars in these terms.</p></div>
